    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1-a4">

                <pb facs="0021" n="11" xml:id="pg11"/>

                <head>Appendix D to HD–85</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Budapest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-03">November 3, 1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[<hi rendition="#italic">The Inter-Allied Military Mission at
                        Budapest to the Supreme Council</hi>]</p>
                <p rendition="#center">Telegram</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">To the Supreme Council—Paris.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Supplement to Telegram No. 740 of October 31.</p>
                <p>The Czecho-Slovak Government subordinates the evacuation of Salgo Tarjan to three
                    conditions: <list>
                        <label>1st</label>
                        <item>—The Hungarians are to be capable of insuring order;</item>
                        <label>2nd</label>
                        <item>—The Hungarians are not to attack the Czecho-Slovaks;</item>
                        <label>3rd</label>
                        <item>—The Hungarian Government is to reimburse the amounts advanced by the
                            Czecho-Slovaks to feed the population.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>The Commission has given the two first assurances. It is of the opinion that the
                    execution of the third condition would be the cause of a new delay which must be
                    avoided at any price. The Budapest mills are without coal.</p>
                <p>The Commission replied to this effect.</p>
                <p>The Commission asks the Supreme Council to use its influence with the Prague
                    Government.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">The President of the Day</hi></closer>
            </div>
